NAME
    touch - create empty files (no-op on existing)

SYNOPSIS
    touch FILE [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
    For each FILE:
      - If FILE doesn't exist, create it as an empty regular file
        with mode 0644.
      - If FILE already exists as a regular file, do nothing
        (AdventFS entries don't carry an mtime today, so there's
        nothing to bump).
      - If FILE exists but isn't a regular file (e.g., it's a
        directory), the underlying sys_fs_write refuses and touch
        reports the failure.

EXAMPLES
    touch hello.txt
    touch a.log b.log c.log

EXIT STATUS
    0   every FILE was touched (or already existed)
    1   at least one FILE could not be touched

SEE ALSO
    cp(1), rm(1)

NOTES
    If/when fs_entry grows an mtime field, touch should start
    bumping it on the existing-file path. Right now there is
    literally nothing to bump.
